› Setup Q1

  abcd needs the key your model service gave you. Where it
  is kept decides who else on this computer can read it.

  - The keychain locks the key with your login.
  - A file in your home folder is readable by every program you run.

  Where should abcd keep the key?

› 1. In the system keychain
     The key is locked with your login; another program must ask to read it.
  2. In a file
     The key sits in your home folder. It works on a machine with no keychain.
  3. Decide later
     Nothing is stored now. abcd asks again at the next setup.

  Now: no key is stored
  Change later: run the setup again and choose the other place
